# ToyVerse Tab — security-research toolkit (open-source, Alpine/pmOS repos)
#
# SCOPE / RESPONSIBLE USE
#   These are standard dual-use security tools (the same ones shipped by Kali,
#   Parrot and BlackArch). Use them ONLY against systems you own or are
#   explicitly authorised in writing to test — e.g. your own ToyVerse nodes,
#   TOYPAY/ToyScan backends, your own Wi-Fi and lab hosts. Unauthorised
#   scanning, cracking or interception is illegal in most countries (in .DE:
#   §§202a–202d StGB). This kit does not include and I will not add exploit
#   payloads, malware, or anything pre-aimed at a third party.
#
# HARDWARE REALITY (read HARDWARE.md)
#   OMAP4430 / 1 GB RAM / armv7 / no usable GPU. So:
#     - No Metasploit, no OpenVAS/Greenbone (not packaged / far too heavy here).
#     - hashcat is CPU-only (no OpenCL GPU) => very slow; prefer john for light jobs.
#     - Internal Wi-Fi almost certainly can't do monitor mode / injection.
#       Wireless auditing needs an external USB adapter that supports it
#       (e.g. Atheros AR9271). Without one, skip the [wireless] group.
#
# INSTALL
#   The install script tries each package and skips any the armv7 repos lack,
#   so a missing tool never breaks the run. Enable community + testing repos
#   first (scripts/harden.sh does this). Groups are tags for that script.

## [recon] network discovery & analysis — light, all should be available
nmap
nmap-scripts
tcpdump
netcat-openbsd
socat
mtr
bind-tools            # dig, nslookup, host
whois
arp-scan
ngrep
hping3
iperf3
masscan               # fast port sweeps (may live in testing)

## [traffic] packet capture / inspection
tshark                # CLI Wireshark (GUI wireshark optional, heavy)
# wireshark           # uncomment for the GTK GUI (RAM-hungry on 1 GB)

## [web] web-app / API testing (your ToyScan / TOYPAY backends)
nikto
sqlmap
whatweb
dirb
gobuster              # go binary, fast dir/dns busting
ffuf                  # go fuzzer
wrk                   # HTTP benchmarking / load
sslscan               # TLS config check
# wpscan              # ruby, only if you run WordPress

## [osint] passive recon
dnsrecon
# theharvester        # python; install via pipx if repo lacks it
# amass               # go; large binary, optional

## [proxy] interception / routing (MITM your own clients)
mitmproxy             # python TLS intercept proxy
proxychains-ng
tor

## [crypto-pw] password / hash work — CPU only here, keep expectations low
john                  # John the Ripper (jumbo recommended if available)
hashcat               # CPU fallback only; slow without GPU
medusa                # parallel login brute-forcer (authorised targets only)
hydra                 # thc-hydra (may live in testing)
crunch                # wordlist generator

## [forensics] firmware / disk / file analysis — great for your own images
binwalk
foremost
sleuthkit
radare2               # reverse engineering / binary analysis

## [wireless] REQUIRES a monitor-mode-capable USB adapter (see note above)
aircrack-ng
iw
wireless-tools
hcxtools
hcxdumptool
reaver

## [scripting] build your own test tooling
py3-scapy             # packet crafting in Python
py3-requests
py3-cryptography
python3
